<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00627</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6c7f3a14-185f-4dc2-b748-4866b2a65b84</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>For questions 1 – 4, use the following scenario to use equations to solve a riddle:</para>
          <para>
            <quote>Here is a riddle: “I am thinking of two numbers that add up to 5.678. The
            difference between them is 9.876. What are the two numbers?”</quote>
         </para>
          <para>Name any pair of numbers whose sum is 5.678.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para>2 and 3.678</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Name any pair of numbers whose difference is 9.876.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para>10 and 0.124</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>The riddle can be represented with two equations. Write the equations.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para>Let \(x\) and \(y\) represent the numbers: \(x+y=5.678\) and \(x-y=9.876\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Solve the riddle. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para>The two numbers are \(7.777\) and \(-2.099\).</para>
          <list>
            <item>Adding the two equations eliminates the \(y\)-variable and gives \(2x=15.554\) or
              \(x=7.777\).</item>
            <item>Substituting this \(x\)-value into either equation gives \(y=-2.099\).</item>
            <item>Graphing the two equations gives two lines that intersect at \((7.777,−2.099)\).</item>
          </list>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="Graph of 2 intersecting lines. Horizontal axis, labeled x, from negative 12 to 12 by 2s. Vertical axis, labeled y, from negative 12 to 12 by 2s. Lines intersect near 8 comma negative 2.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_02_01.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
